  <static seed="115" source="Library/Mizzou/Matrix_Theory/HW_6/prob_1.pg">
    <statement><p>Let <m>{ \mathbf{u}_1, \mathbf{u}_2, \mathbf{u}_3 }</m> be an orthonormal basis for an inner product space <m>V</m>. If</p>
<p><me>\mathbf{v} = a \mathbf{u}_1 + b \mathbf{u}_2 + c \mathbf{u}_3</me></p>
<p>is so that <m>\|\mathbf{v}\| = 91</m>, <m>\mathbf{v}</m> is orthogonal to <m>\mathbf{u}_3</m>, and <m>\langle \mathbf{v},\mathbf{u}_2 \rangle = -91</m>, find the possible values for <m>a</m>, <m>b</m>, and <m>c</m>.</p>
<p><m>a =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/>, <m>b =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/>, <m>c =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-91</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><alert>Solution:</alert> One checks by direct computation that</p>
<p><m>a = 0</m>, <m>b = -91</m>, <m>c = 0</m></p>
<p>must hold.</p>
</solution>
